{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558652994,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf94d53ffebzXtwlVhQAwWQy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407f1f1001ANOCGuQ4CS2ZlC","sessionID":"ses_e2bf94d53ffebzXtwlVhQAwWQy","messageID":"msg_1d407e51e001dwRA2DXhQ9WTN9","type":"tool","id":"call_01_w68d9dryuvuitemz40iin1dh","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs","limit":80},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, lines 1-80\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Shipped Instruction Check Engine\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // A repository that took the shipped instruction template can be in any of seven\n8: // states, and nothing in it says which one. Its shipped sections may be current, one\n9: // release behind, or edited in place; its own content may sit in the marked block or be\n10: // scattered between shipped sections; it may have no root document at all. Without that\n11: // answer there is nothing to plan a rewrite from, and no way to tell a safe replacement\n12: // from one that would drop a line somebody wrote. So this engine reports, per row and\n13: // without writing a byte, what the repository holds against the manifest.\n14: //\n15: // Three of the twelve rows are answers this engine must not invent. The delivery budget\n16: // and its anchors belong to the rule-copy canary, the Cursor pointer block belongs to\n17: // the gate 1 sync, and the router belongs to the repo-rules checker. Each already has\n18: // tests and an owner, so each is run as a child process and its own lines are carried\n19: // into the report; re-deriving any of them here would be a second opinion that drifts\n20: // from the first. The rest are pure classifiers over one read of the target tree.\n21: //\n22: // The run is read-only by construction: the only paths it opens for reading are under\n23: // the target root plus the manifest, and the three child tools it runs are read-only\n24: // modes. A repository that cannot be classified at all (no manifest, no target\n25: // directory, an unreadable root document) is a failed precondition and exits 2, because\n26: // an empty report would read like a clean one.\n27: //\n28: // Usage: agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <path>] [--source] [--json]\n29: //   --root <dir>      classify this repository instead of the one this script ships in\n30: //   --manifest <path> read this manifest instead of the shipped one\n31: //   --source          run the template-purity row even outside the source repository\n32: //   --json            print one JSON object instead of the text report\n33: // Exit codes: 0 nothing to report, 1 at least one finding or an unproven row,\n34: //             2 a precondition failed\n35: \n36: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: // 1. IMPORTS\n38: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n39: \n40: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n41: const fs = require('node:fs');\n42: const path = require('node:path');\n43: \n44: const {\n45:   classifyBody,\n46:   deliveryAnchorEnd,\n47:   matchSections,\n48:   segment,\n49: } = require('./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs');\n50: const { sourceStatus } = require('./agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n51: \n52: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: // 2. CONSTANTS\n54: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n55: \n56: const TAG = '[agents-md-check]';\n57: const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../..');\n58: const MANIFEST_PATH = path.resolve(__dirname, '../assets/agents-md-manifest.json');\n59: const GENERATOR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n60: // The router checker ships beside the skill that authors rules, and the manifest links\n61: // it only through the router's own row, so its path is named here once.\n62: const REPO_RULES_CHECKER = path.resolve(\n63:   REPO_ROOT,\n64:   '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs',\n65: );\n66: // The checker's own tag prefix. Matching on it is what keeps this row a carrier of that\n67: // tool's verdict instead of a second implementation of its checks.\n68: const REPO_RULES_TAG = '[repo-rules-check]';\n69: const USAGE = 'Usage: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <path>] [--source] [--json]';\n70: const TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS = 120000;\n71: \n72: // A repository where fewer than half the shipped sections survive is carrying its own\n73: // document, not a copy of the template. Above the line the question becomes which parts\n74: // of the template are still there, which is a per-section answer.\n75: const FOREIGN_SHARE = 0.5;\n76: \n77: const PASS = 'PASS';\n78: const FINDING = 'FINDING';\n79: const UNKNOWN = 'UNKNOWN';\n80: const INFO = 'INFO';\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs, lines 1-80\n1: #!/usr/bin/env node\n2: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n3: // MODULE: Shipped Instruction Check Engine\n4: // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n5: 'use strict';\n6: \n7: // A repository that took the shipped instruction template can be in any of seven\n8: // states, and nothing in it says which one. Its shipped sections may be current, one\n9: // release behind, or edited in place; its own content may sit in the marked block or be\n10: // scattered between shipped sections; it may have no root document at all. Without that\n11: // answer there is nothing to plan a rewrite from, and no way to tell a safe replacement\n12: // from one that would drop a line somebody wrote. So this engine reports, per row and\n13: // without writing a byte, what the repository holds against the manifest.\n14: //\n15: // Three of the twelve rows are answers this engine must not invent. The delivery budget\n16: // and its anchors belong to the rule-copy canary, the Cursor pointer block belongs to\n17: // the gate 1 sync, and the router belongs to the repo-rules checker. Each already has\n18: // tests and an owner, so each is run as a child process and its own lines are carried\n19: // into the report; re-deriving any of them here would be a second opinion that drifts\n20: // from the first. The rest are pure classifiers over one read of the target tree.\n21: //\n22: // The run is read-only by construction: the only paths it opens for reading are under\n23: // the target root plus the manifest, and the three child tools it runs are read-only\n24: // modes. A repository that cannot be classified at all (no manifest, no target\n25: // directory, an unreadable root document) is a failed precondition and exits 2, because\n26: // an empty report would read like a clean one.\n27: //\n28: // Usage: agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <path>] [--source] [--json]\n29: //   --root <dir>      classify this repository instead of the one this script ships in\n30: //   --manifest <path> read this manifest instead of the shipped one\n31: //   --source          run the template-purity row even outside the source repository\n32: //   --json            print one JSON object instead of the text report\n33: // Exit codes: 0 nothing to report, 1 at least one finding or an unproven row,\n34: //             2 a precondition failed\n35: \n36: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n37: // 1. IMPORTS\n38: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n39: \n40: const { spawnSync } = require('node:child_process');\n41: const fs = require('node:fs');\n42: const path = require('node:path');\n43: \n44: const {\n45:   classifyBody,\n46:   deliveryAnchorEnd,\n47:   matchSections,\n48:   segment,\n49: } = require('./lib/agents-md-sections.cjs');\n50: const { sourceStatus } = require('./agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n51: \n52: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n53: // 2. CONSTANTS\n54: // ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n55: \n56: const TAG = '[agents-md-check]';\n57: const REPO_ROOT = path.resolve(__dirname, '../../../..');\n58: const MANIFEST_PATH = path.resolve(__dirname, '../assets/agents-md-manifest.json');\n59: const GENERATOR = path.resolve(__dirname, 'agents-md-manifest.cjs');\n60: // The router checker ships beside the skill that authors rules, and the manifest links\n61: // it only through the router's own row, so its path is named here once.\n62: const REPO_RULES_CHECKER = path.resolve(\n63:   REPO_ROOT,\n64:   '.skilled/skills/sk-doc/sk-create-repo-rule/scripts/check-repo-rules.cjs',\n65: );\n66: // The checker's own tag prefix. Matching on it is what keeps this row a carrier of that\n67: // tool's verdict instead of a second implementation of its checks.\n68: const REPO_RULES_TAG = '[repo-rules-check]';\n69: const USAGE = 'Usage: node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs [--root <dir>] [--manifest <path>] [--source] [--json]';\n70: const TOOL_TIMEOUT_MS = 120000;\n71: \n72: // A repository where fewer than half the shipped sections survive is carrying its own\n73: // document, not a copy of the template. Above the line the question becomes which parts\n74: // of the template are still there, which is a per-section answer.\n75: const FOREIGN_SHARE = 0.5;\n76: \n77: const PASS = 'PASS';\n78: const FINDING = 'FINDING';\n79: const UNKNOWN = 'UNKNOWN';\n80: const INFO = 'INFO';\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs\", \"limit\": 80}"},"time":{"start":1794558652913,"end":1794558652994}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794558653007,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf94d53ffebzXtwlVhQAwWQy","part":{"partID":"prt_1d407f1a8001BlYghZ0yM4YXu3","sessionID":"ses_e2bf94d53ffebzXtwlVhQAwWQy","messageID":"msg_1d407e51e001dwRA2DXhQ9WTN9","type":"tool","id":"call_00_esqttl0jeqd62bjdn4b7u6tk","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && jq '.runtime_copies' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json 2>/dev/null || find .skilled -name 'agents-md-manifest.json' -maxdepth 6"},"output":"[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"CLAUDE.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"absent\",\n      \"symlink\",\n      \"pointer\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Claude reads the root document directly, and Cursor and Hermes load both files, so a full copy either double-loads or drifts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".codex/AGENTS.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"absent\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Codex loads the root document as project instructions, so a second copy under its own directory is a copy nothing reads.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".cursorrules\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"absent\"\n    ],\n    \"report_only\": true,\n    \"why\": \"A legacy path that Cursor and Hermes still read; reported so a stale copy is visible, never written because it is not where edits belong.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"gate1-block-in-sync\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Cursor and Devin read this rule on its own, so it carries a generated copy of the gate 1 lookup line rather than a hand-kept one.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"mirrored-when-block-non-empty\",\n      \"absent-when-block-empty\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Devin never sees past the delivery prefix of the root document, so a non-empty repository block needs this second surface to reach it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \"~/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"reported-only\"\n    ],\n    \"report_only\": true,\n    \"why\": \"A path outside the repository: reported because a symlink to the root document changes what every session loads, never written.\"\n  }\n]\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"[\n  {\n    \"path\": \"CLAUDE.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"absent\",\n      \"symlink\",\n      \"pointer\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Claude reads the root document directly, and Cursor and Hermes load both files, so a full copy either double-loads or drifts.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".codex/AGENTS.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"absent\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Codex loads the root document as project instructions, so a second copy under its own directory is a copy nothing reads.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".cursorrules\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"absent\"\n    ],\n    \"report_only\": true,\n    \"why\": \"A legacy path that Cursor and Hermes still read; reported so a stale copy is visible, never written because it is not where edits belong.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".cursor/rules/skill-routing.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"gate1-block-in-sync\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Cursor and Devin read this rule on its own, so it carries a generated copy of the gate 1 lookup line rather than a hand-kept one.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \".cursor/rules/repo-local.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"mirrored-when-block-non-empty\",\n      \"absent-when-block-empty\"\n    ],\n    \"why\": \"Devin never sees past the delivery prefix of the root document, so a non-empty repository block needs this second surface to reach it.\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"path\": \"~/.claude/CLAUDE.md\",\n    \"expect\": [\n      \"reported-only\"\n    ],\n    \"report_only\": true,\n    \"why\": \"A path outside the repository: reported because a symlink to the root document changes what every session loads, never written.\"\n  }\n]\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\": \"cd /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research && jq '.runtime_copies' .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/agents-md-manifest.json 2>/dev/null || find .skilled -name 'agents-md-manifest.json' -maxdepth 6\"}"},"time":{"start":1794558652840,"end":1794558653007}}}}
