{"type":"text","timestamp":1794558734004,"sessionID":"ses_e2bf94d53ffebzXtwlVhQAwWQy","part":{"id":"prt_1d40923b4002qO5YieHRTkFT9B","sessionID":"ses_e2bf94d53ffebzXtwlVhQAwWQy","messageID":"msg_1d4090f5700139VoCQhUmIZSsy","type":"text","text":"T024 is complete.\n\n**Files written**\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs` — added the case `a symlinked copy where the checklist expects no file is a finding` on the `pure` fixture: creates `.codex/AGENTS.md` as a symlink to `../AGENTS.md` and asserts the A10 entry is `FINDING` with kind `symlink where none belongs`.\n- `.skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs` — in `copyVerdict`'s symlink branch, `expectsAbsent` now returns `{ state: FINDING, kind: 'symlink where none belongs', detail: 'links to <link>, where the checklist expects no file' }` before `pointsAtRoot` is read.\n\n**Verify output**\n\nBefore the change, the new case failed on `PASS` as the task predicted:\n\n```\nℹ tests 41\nℹ pass 40\nℹ fail 1\n\n✖ a symlinked copy where the checklist expects no file is a finding\n  AssertionError [ERR_ASSERTION]: a link at an absent-only path is not a pass\n  'PASS' !== 'FINDING'\n```\n\nAfter the change, `node --test .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/tests/agents-md-check.test.cjs`:\n\n```\nℹ tests 41\nℹ suites 0\nℹ pass 41\nℹ fail 0\nℹ cancelled 0\nℹ skipped 0\nℹ todo 0\n```\n\nAnd `node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/agents-md-check.cjs | rg -c \"^STATUS=OK\"` printed `1`. The run also exits 0 with `A10 runtime copies: 6/6 copies as expected   (PASS)` and `STATUS=OK rows=12 findings=0 unknown=0`.\n\n**Not done:** nothing outstanding. Only the two named files are modified (`git status --short` shows exactly those two), the `tasks.md` checkbox is untouched, and no git state was changed.\n\n**Operator next step:** the orchestrator should mark T024 `[x]` in `tasks.md` and run T025 next in the WG5 lane.","time":{"start":1794558731188,"end":1794558734004}}}
